  'sapa-yopa-bikers-rally-meropa-26-29-november-2026-11-01',
  'Thousands of bikers expected at Meropa for the Sapa Yopa rally later this month',
  'Tourism', '2026-11-01', 'Review Online', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/review-online/news-headlines/local-news/2026/11/01/sapa-yopa-rally-to-draw-5-000-bikers-to-polokwane/',
  'The Sapa Yopa Motorcycle Club will host its 19th annual rally at Meropa Casino from 26 to 29 November, with more than 5 000 bikers expected.',
  'Polokwane is preparing for a big motorcycle weekend. The Sapa Yopa Motorcycle Club is staging its 19th yearly rally at the Meropa Casino complex between 26 and 29 November, and organisers expect over 5 000 riders travelling in from around the SADC region.

According to Review Online, the opening day, 26 November, brings a golf tournament and an evening gala dinner. The main rally is on the Saturday and features a group ride from the venue out to Seshego, while a closing party takes place on 29 November. A ticketing listing for the event describes four days of bike races and live music at the Go-Kart venue inside Meropa Casino in Ivypark, with tickets starting at R200.

The club says this year''s theme honours electricity linemen who helped restore stability to the power supply. It also says the event is meant for the wider community and aims to promote motorcycle culture and tourism in Limpopo, with vendor stalls and music on the programme.

On the roads, the club says it is coordinating with the municipality and the city''s Joint Operations Committee so that the weekend runs smoothly and traffic rules are respected. Motorists in the Ivypark and Seshego areas may want to allow extra time around the mass ride on the Saturday.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/review-online/news-headlines/local-news/2026/11/01/sapa-yopa-rally-to-draw-5-000-bikers-to-polokwane/", "https://computicket-boxoffice.com/e/sapa-yopa-south-africa-Txk6Pu"]',
  'agent'
);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news (
  slug, title, category, published_date, source_name, source_url,
  summary, body, image_url, image_credit, image_source, verification_json, source
) VALUES (
  'polokwane-city-head-coach-resigns-health-2026-11-03',
  'Polokwane City head coach resigns after nine league matches, citing his health',
  'Sport', '2026-11-03', 'iDiski Times', 'https://www.idiskitimes.co.za/betway-premiership/moloto-confirms-shock-polokwane-decision/',
  'Polokwane City head coach Willy Moloto has resigned to focus on his health, leaving the Betway Premiership side 11th on the log with eight points.',
  'Polokwane City are looking for a new head coach after Willy Moloto confirmed on 3 November that he has resigned from the Betway Premiership club.

Moloto has been away from the dugout because of health problems and told iDiski Times he wanted to focus on his recovery. He said it did not feel right to keep drawing a salary while he was unable to work. He was in charge for nine league matches, with one win, five draws and three losses, according to Africa Soccer.

The club sits 11th on the league log with eight points. Africa Soccer reports that the club now has to find a replacement for the rest of the season, and that its next league match is against Durban City in late November. At the time of writing no permanent successor had been announced.

For supporters in Polokwane, the change comes during a break in the league calendar, which gives the club some time to make an appointment before the next fixture.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.idiskitimes.co.za/betway-premiership/moloto-confirms-shock-polokwane-decision/", "https://africasoccer.com/polokwane-city-coach-willy-moloto-resigns-after-nine-matches/"]',
  'agent'
);
